    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d763">

                <pb facs="0720" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/4540</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 19, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your Department’s request by
                    telephone for information relative to reports that the British S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Oxonian</hi> had sunk a submarine about December 28, I
                    have the honor to enclose herewith a copy of a letter dated the 17th instant,
                    from the collector of customs at Norfolk, and a copy of the statement of the
                    master.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to advise me what instructions you desire given to the collector
                    relative to the clearance of this vessel.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Secretary.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Peters</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d763-a1.xml" xpointer="d763-a1"/>
            </div>
